# LF everywhere, in the repo and in the working tree. `text=auto eol=lf` rather than a bare
# `text=auto`: the latter stores LF but checks out CRLF on Windows, so every tool that writes LF
# leaves the working tree disagreeing with what is committed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Correctness overrides, not style: these two formats require a specific ending to execute.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.sh text eol=lf
# Demo files live in Git LFS (migrated 2026-08-07, when the corpus went from one 8.9 MB
# file to three totalling ~131 MB). Plain git would keep every byte of every version in
# history forever, and every clone would pay for it; LFS stores a ~130-byte pointer here
# and fetches blobs on demand. Anyone cloning needs `git lfs install` first.
# The LFS filter line below is further down, written by `git lfs track`.
# Phase 2/3 asset formats, listed ahead of time so none of them can be mangled on first commit.
*.bsp binary
*.mdl binary
*.vtf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.dem filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
